# Text normalisation.
# Source and documentation files are stored LF in the blob and checked out LF in the
# worktree, on every platform. Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (set at system level on
# this host) checks them out CRLF, so any artifact that fingerprints worktree bytes
# cannot be verified from a fresh clone. Fixing this does NOT change existing blobs; it
# only makes future checkouts agree with them.
*.py text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# Raw external-data snapshots must never be line-ending-normalized: their
# identity is the byte-for-byte SHA-256 pinned in MANIFEST.json, and
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise corrupt them on fresh clones.
research/orbital-mechanics/experiments/jplValidation/reference/*.txt -text
research/orbital-mechanics/experiments/eclipseTiming/reference/*.txt -text
research/orbital-mechanics/experiments/lunisolarVerification/reference/*.txt -text
# MANIFEST.json files are checksum manifests: their pinned SHA-256 values are also
# line-ending sensitive, so they are `-text` too. This block MUST come after the
# `*.json text eol=lf` line above -- gitattributes is last-match-wins.
research/orbital-mechanics/experiments/jplValidation/reference/MANIFEST.json -text
research/orbital-mechanics/experiments/eclipseTiming/reference/MANIFEST.json -text
research/orbital-mechanics/experiments/lunisolarVerification/reference/MANIFEST.json -text
# Byte-pinned DE441 Sun/Moon vectors (mission_lunisolar_closure). These were previously
# protected only by `mission_lunisolar_closure/.gitattributes`, whose patterns are
# resolved RELATIVE TO THAT DIRECTORY and were therefore written in a repo-root-relative
# form that matched nothing: `git check-attr text` reported `unspecified` for all of
# them. The patterns are repeated here, at the root, where they resolve correctly.
# `tests/test_reference_data_provenance.py` asserts this does not regress.
research/orbital-mechanics/missions/mission_lunisolar_closure/reference/*.txt -text
research/orbital-mechanics/missions/mission_lunisolar_closure/reference/per_chunk/*.txt -text
research/orbital-mechanics/missions/mission_lunisolar_closure/reference/MANIFEST.json -text
# Byte-pinned DE441 Sun/Moon vectors (mission_secular_identification, acquired
# 2026-10-04, span 2026-01-01 -> 2064-01-01, 13880 daily rows). Patterns here
# resolve against the repository ROOT, which is why they are written out in full.
# Guarded by src/lab_utils/tests/test_reference_data_provenance.py.
research/orbital-mechanics/missions/mission_secular_identification/reference/*.txt -text
research/orbital-mechanics/missions/mission_secular_identification/reference/MANIFEST.json -text
